**No dependency of this project is under a copyleft or a proprietary licence, and
that is a rule rather than an accident.** tests/test_licences.py holds it: every
dependency named in pyproject.toml or in a Cargo.toml under native/ must appear
in docs/licences.toml with a licence from a permissive allowlist, so adding one
that does not fails the suite rather than being noticed later. The rule exists
because the alternative is remembering, and this project's standard is that a
rule nothing enforces is a rule nobody keeps.

One consequence is recorded here because it decides an engineering choice rather
than a legal one: **redistributing NVIDIA's CUDA runtime libraries is governed by
NVIDIA's licence and not by an open-source one**, so a GPU build that has to ship
cuBLAS or cuDNN is out. Where GPU acceleration is wanted, the Vulkan path is the
one that redistributes nothing proprietary.

